@4.25 DOS.INC.BL -- a drive command, and a test for a file
.
=4.25 DOS.INC.BL -- A DRIVE COMMAND, AND A TEST FOR A FILE
.
=DESCRIPTION
.
.Two verbs on the drive's command channel. DOSX sends a command and reads the
.drive's answer. DOSX.EXISTS tests whether a file opens. Each also has a
.GOSUB entry that takes its argument in a variable.
.
.It is the smaller alternative to FILEIO.INC.BL (SEC 4.15). A program
.includes one or the other, not both. It needs GPB.INC.BL ahead of it and
.includes nothing.
.
.DOS.DEVICE is the drive. A call with it 0 uses 8 and leaves it 8.
.
.After either verb, DOS.ERR is the drive's error number and DOS.MSG$ its
.message. DOS.ERR under DOS.OKMAX, 20, is success.
.
.Nothing in the module needs the GP block. GP.FN brings it in, 1,536 bytes.
.GP.SUB and GOSUB leave it out (SEC 3.11).
.
=IN THIS SECTION
.
>108|4.25.1 DOSX -- send a command, read the answer
>109|4.25.2 DOSX.EXISTS -- whether a file opens
.
